  "title": "Strawberry Jam",
  "description": "This strawberry jam recipe is easy to make without pectin. Packed with fruity flavor, this delicious homemade jam lets you enjoy summer all year long!",
  "authors": [
    "Katharine"
  ],
  "date_published": "2001-07-22T14:23:42-04:00",
  "date_modified": "2026-07-28T12:34:26-04:00",
  "prep_time": "PT20M",
  "cook_time": "PT20M",
  "total_time": "PT40M",
  "yield": [
    "40",
    "5 cups of jam"
  ],
  "categories": [
    "Jam / Jelly"
  ],
  "cuisines": [
    "American"
  ],
  "regions": [
    "American"
  ],
  "breadcrumbs": [],
  "keywords": [
    "publisher-tested"
  ],
  "ingredients": [
    "2 pounds fresh strawberries, hulled",
    "4 cups white sugar",
    "0.25 cup lemon juice"
  ],
  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Gather all ingredients.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/hxtODkW7b6hdbSWhQfOz5EYCL34=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/AR-RM-38410-strawberry-jam-ddmfs-ingredients-3x4-7b90ec514b3b4a56a36a70f8495e5942.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/38410/step_01.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Crush strawberries in a wide bowl in batches until you have 4 cups of mashed strawberries.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/qeUpPsYWm4yxFAv-oH6LWDNuLAA=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/AR-RM-38410-strawberry-jam-ddmfs-step1-3x4-ae2e873873db4b5b98736d3bf63ef4b6.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/38410/step_02.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Combine mashed strawberries, sugar, and lemon juice in a heavy-bottomed saucepan; stir over low heat until sugar is dissolved.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/LtEaVoRGu3VfLAD06AJL8eLpZuE=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/AR-RM-38410-strawberry-jam-ddmfs-step2-3x4-0eff9e2d259343fd89db2a32b39f71fe.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/38410/step_03.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Increase heat to high, and bring the mixture to a full rolling boil. Continue to boil, stirring often, until the mixture reaches 220 degrees F (105 degrees C).",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/Ed_958EO_gyavMkgYdxATT6B1xI=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/AR-RM-38410-strawberry-jam-ddmfs-step3-3x4-8f2acc96ff82456e9165a486fae6109d.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/38410/step_04.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Check doneness after 10 to 15 minutes by dropping a small spoonful of jam onto a frozen plate. Let sit for 1 to 2 minutes; if jam appears to gel, it is ready. Continue cooking if jam appears thin and runny.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/BFA9vryLE547c-Z07d7gC-nOJFs=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/AR-RM-38410-strawberry-jam-ddmfs-step4-3x4-5f8db77a37fa4e628cde0c637911f138.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/38410/step_05.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Transfer jam into hot sterile jars, filling to within 1/4 inch of the top. Top with lids and screw rings on tightly.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/DGlkt52ge5Ex11giEgM83lA-N9w=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/AR-RM-38410-strawberry-jam-ddmfs-step5-3x4-6ffabf8c56ea4c8ebb18722bbb336f0a.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/38410/step_06.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Place a rack in the bottom of a large stockpot and fill it halfway with water. Bring to a boil and lower jars 2 inches apart into the boiling water using a holder.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/cwqBr75womvjuhXrb3CLKSrzt2Q=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/AR-RM-38410-strawberry-jam-ddmfs-step6-3x4-89a8d2e43ffe4445860e46fa24cb1cbf.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/38410/step_07.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Pour in more boiling water to cover jars by at least 1 inch. Bring to a rolling boil, cover, and process for 10 minutes.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/Ntg_WA3HmklxhLWPLzkDB3LZL2U=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/AR-RM-38410-strawberry-jam-ddmfs-step7-3x4-ee232b3a6d4e44f69b7fce7b8ec7fb8a.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/38410/step_08.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Remove the jars from the stockpot and let rest, several inches apart, for 12 to 24 hours. Store in a cool, dark area.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/OYnDK4SEzY7qysDS5euG2w1od4A=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/AR-RM-38410-strawberry-jam-ddmfs-step8-3x4-e48bdb042829450cad9ba5361f66132b.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/38410/step_09.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Serve and enjoy!",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/nQwMe2m0ubpwoPtkdTL3ykzOueM=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/AR-RM-38410-strawberry-jam-ddmfs-3x4-f0c842d7fed7479abe8f45f541a097a5.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/38410/step_10.webp"
    }
  ],
